hadiths[77]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1721","On the authority of Jabir ibn Samurah, who said: Umar addressed the people at Al-Jabiyah and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) stood in a position like this one of mine and said: ""Be good to my companions, then those who come after them, then those who come after them. Then there will come a people who will swear oaths before being asked to swear, and will give testimony before being asked to testify. Whoever among you wishes to attain the vastness of Paradise, let him hold fast to the congregation, for Satan is with the solitary one, and he is farther from two. And let no man be alone with a woman, for the third of them is Satan. And whoever among you is pleased by his good deed and saddened by his evil deed, then he is a believer."""
"1722","On the authority of Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from his grandfather (Abdullah ibn Amr), who said: I witnessed Allah's Messenger (peace be upon him) when the delegation of Hawazin came to him. They said: ""O Muhammad! We are a people and a clan, so bestow favor upon us, may Allah bestow favor upon you. For there has befallen us a calamity that is not hidden from you."" He said: ""Choose between your women, your wealth, and your children."" They said: ""You have given us the choice between our honor and our wealth; we choose our children."" He said: ""As for what belongs to me and to the Banu Abdul Muttalib, it is yours. So when I pray the Zuhr prayer, say: 'We seek intercession through Allah's Messenger with the believers, and through the believers with Allah's Messenger (peace be upon him) regarding our women and our children.'"" So they did that. Then Allah's Messenger (peace be upon him) said: ""As for what belongs to me and to the Banu Abdul Muttalib, it is yours."" The Muhajirun said: ""What belongs to us is for Allah's Messenger (peace be upon him)."" The Ansar said the same. Uyayna ibn Badr said: ""As for what belongs to me and to the Banu Fazara, no."" Al-Aqra' ibn Habis said: ""As for me and the Banu Tamim, no."" Abbas ibn Mirdas said: ""As for me and the Banu Sulaym, no."" The two tribes said: ""You lie; rather it is for Allah's Messenger (peace be upon him)."" Allah's Messenger (peace be upon him) said: ""O people, return to them their women and their children. Whoever holds onto anything from the booty (fay'), for him there are six camels from the first thing Allah grants us as booty."" Then he mounted his riding camel, and the people clung to him, saying: ""Distribute our booty among us,"" until they forced him against a samura tree, and his cloak was snatched away. He said: ""O people, return my cloak to me. By Allah, if you had camels equal in number to the trees of Tihama, I would have distributed them among you. Then you would not find me miserly, nor cowardly, nor a liar."" Then he drew near to his camel, took a hair from its hump, placed it between his forefinger and middle finger, raised it, and said: ""O people, I have nothing from this booty, nor this hair, except the fifth (khums), and the fifth is returned to you. So return the needle and the thread. For stealing from the booty (ghulul) will be a source of shame, fire, and disgrace for its people on the Day of Resurrection."""
"1723","[AI-translation] He (peace be upon him) said: The thing I fear most for my ummah is the misguided leaders."
"1724","[AI-translation] The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: If allegiance is pledged to two caliphs, then kill the latter of them."
"1725","[AI-translation] Khudri, elevated to the Prophet: When three people go out on a journey, they should appoint one of them as their leader."
"1726","[AI-translation] From 'Alqamah bin Wa'il bin Hujr, from his father, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) while a man asked him, saying: ""What do you think if there are rulers over us who deny us our right and demand their right?"" The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""Hear and obey, for upon them is what they have been burdened with, and upon you is what you have been burdened with."
"1727","[AI-translation] Ashja'i, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) addressed us at midday while he was awe-stricken, and he said: ""Obey me as long as I am among you, and hold fast to the Book of Allah, Mighty and Majestic. Make lawful what it makes lawful, and forbid what it forbids."
"1728","On the authority of Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) stood among us delivering a sermon, and part of his sermon was that he said: ""Behold, I am about to be summoned and I shall respond, and there will succeed me governors who will speak what they know and act according to what they recognize, and obedience to them is obedience. You will remain thus for a time. Then there will succeed you governors after them who will speak what they do not know and act according to what they do not recognize. Whoever advises them, assists them, and supports them, those have perished and caused others to perish. Associate with them bodily, but oppose them with your deeds, and bear witness that the good-doer is a good-doer, and the evil-doer is an evil-doer."""
"1729","Abdur-Rahman ibn Shimasah said: I came to Aisha to ask her about something. She said: ""Where are you from?"" I said: ""A man from the people of Egypt."" She said: ""How was your governor for you in this expedition of yours?"" He said: ""We did not find any fault with him. If a man's camel died, he would give him a camel; if his slave died, he would give him a slave; and if he needed provisions, he would give him provisions."" She said: ""Nevertheless, what he did to Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr, my brother, will not prevent me from telling you what I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying in this house of mine: 'O Allah, whoever takes charge of any affair of my Ummah and makes it difficult for them, make it difficult for him; and whoever takes charge of any affair of my Ummah and is gentle with them, be gentle with him.'"""
"1730","[AI-translation] From Anas, elevated to the Prophet: Indeed, Allah will question every shepherd about what He entrusted to him, whether he safeguarded it or lost it, until a man is questioned about his household."
"1731","Abu Hurayrah reported: The Prophet (peace be upon him) said to Abu al-Haytham: ""Do you have a servant?"" He said: ""No."" He said: ""Then when a captive comes to us, come to us."" Then the Prophet (peace be upon him) was brought two captives, without a third with them. Abu al-Haytham came to him, and the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""Choose one of them."" He said: ""O Messenger of Allah, choose for me."" The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""The consultant is trusted. Take this one, for I saw him praying, and treat him well."" His wife said: ""You will not fulfill what the Prophet (peace be upon him) said about him unless you free him."" He said: ""He is free."" The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""Allah did not send a prophet nor a caliph except that he has two advisors: an advisor who commands him to good and forbids him from evil, and an advisor who does not spare him corruption. And whoever is protected from the evil advisor has been protected."""
"1732","[AI-translation] From Salim, from his father ('Abdullah bin 'Umar), that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) said while he was on the pulpit: ""If you find fault with the leadership of—he meant: Usamah bin Zayd—then you have already found fault with the leadership of his father before him. By Allah! He was indeed worthy of it. By Allah! He was the most beloved of people to me. By Allah! This one is indeed worthy of it—he meant Usamah bin Zayd—and by Allah! He is the most beloved of them to me after him. So I advise you concerning him, for he is among your righteous."
"1733","[AI-translation] From 'Awf bin Malik, from the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family), he said: ""If you wish, I will inform you about leadership and what it is. Its first stage is blame, its second stage is regret, and its third stage is punishment on the Day of Resurrection, except for the one who acts justly. But how can he act justly with his close relatives?"
"1734","[AI-translation] Hasan that 'A'idh bin 'Amr - and he was from the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) - entered upon 'Ubaidullah bin Ziyad and said: O my son! I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) say: The worst of shepherds is Al-Hatamah. So beware lest you be among them. He said to him: Sit, for you are but from the chaff of the companions of Muhammad (peace be upon him)! He said: Did they have any chaff? Chaff only came after them, and among others!"
"1735","[AI-translation] From Jubair bin Mut'im who said: A woman came to the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) and he ordered her to return to him. She said: What if I come and do not find you? - as if she meant death. He (peace be upon him) said: If you do not find me, then come to Abu Bakr."
"1736","[AI-translation] From Abu Musa who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) stood at the door of a house in which was a group of Quraysh. He stood and grasped the ring of the door, then said: Is there anyone in the house except a Qurashi? He said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, other than so-and-so, the son of our sister. He said: The son of the sister of a people is from them. Then he said: This matter will be in Quraysh as long as when they are asked for mercy, they show mercy, when they judge, they act justly, and when they divide, they do so equitably. Whoever among them does not do that, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all the people. No expiation and no ransom will be accepted from him."
"1737","Al-Zuhri said: Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im used to narrate that it reached Mu'awiyah, while they were with him in a delegation from Quraysh, that Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As was narrating that there would be a king from Qahtan. So he became angry, stood up, praised Allah as He deserves, then said: ""As for what follows: It has reached me that some men among you narrate hadiths that are not in the Book of Allah nor are they reported from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family). Those are your ignorant ones. So beware of the wishful thinking that misleads its people. Verily, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family) say: 'This matter (authority) is in Quraysh; none opposes them except Allah throws him on his face, as long as they establish the religion.'"""
"1738","Al-Miqdām ibn Maʿdī Karib al-Kindī reported: He sat with ʿUbādah ibn al-Ṣāmit, Abū al-Dardāʾ, and al-Ḥārith ibn Muʿāwiyah al-Kindī, and they recalled the ḥadīth of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Abū al-Dardāʾ said to ʿUbādah: ""O ʿUbādah, the words of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the expedition of such-and-such concerning the matter of the fifths (khumus)."" ʿUbādah said: ""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led them in prayer during their expedition beside a camel from the division (al-maqsim). When he gave the taslīm, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood up, took a single hair between his two fingertips, and said: 'This belongs to your spoils of war, and I have no share in it except my share alongside you, except the fifth—and the fifth is returned to you. So bring forth the thread and the needle, and what is greater than that and what is smaller. And do not commit ghulūl (embezzlement of spoils), for ghulūl is Fire and disgrace upon its perpetrators in this world and the Hereafter. And strive against people in the cause of Allah—Blessed and Exalted—near and far, and fear not in Allah the reproach of any reproacher. And uphold the limits of Allah in residence and travel. And strive in the way of Allah, for jihād is a gate from the gates of Paradise, tremendous, by which Allah—Blessed and Exalted—delivers from grief and anxiety.'"""
"1739","[AI-translation] From Sharid bin Suwaid who said: There was in the delegation of Thaqif a man with leprosy. The Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) sent to him: We have already pledged allegiance to you, so return."
"1740","[AI-translation] From Abu Musa who said: I entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family), I and two men from my paternal cousins. One of the two men said: O Messenger of Allah! Appoint us over some of what Allah has put you in charge of. And the other said the same. He said: He said: By Allah, we do not appoint to this work anyone who asks for it, nor anyone who is eager for it."
"1741","[AI-translation] Ansari who said: The Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) sent me as a collector of charity, then he said: Go, Abu Mas'ud, and let me not find you on the Day of Resurrection coming with a camel of the charity camels on your back braying, which you have misappropriated. He said: Then I will not go. He said: Then I will not compel you."
"1742","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah from the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) who said: You will eagerly seek leadership, and it will be a cause of regret (and sorrow) on the Day of Resurrection. So what an excellent wet-nurse it is, and what an evil weaning it is!"
"1743","[AI-translation] From 'Abdullah, narrated as elevated (to the Prophet): There will rule over your affairs after me men who extinguish the Sunnah, introduce innovation, and delay the prayer from its times. Ibn Mas'ud said: What about me if I encounter them? He said: There is no obedience to the one who disobeys Allah, O Ibn Umm 'Abd. He said this three times."
"1744","Abdullah ibn Buraydah narrated: I heard my father Buraydah say: We besieged Khaybar, and Abu Bakr took the banner but it was not conquered for him. Then Umar took it the next day and returned without it being conquered for him. The people suffered severe hardship and difficulty that day. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""I will give my banner tomorrow to a man who loves Allah and His Messenger, and whom Allah and His Messenger love; he will not return until it is conquered for him."" We spent the night with our souls at ease, knowing that the conquest would be tomorrow. When morning came, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed the dawn prayer, then stood up and called for the banner while the people were in their ranks. There was none of us who had a position with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ except that he hoped to be the bearer of the banner. He called for Ali ibn Abi Talib, who was suffering from an eye ailment. He spat in his eyes and wiped them, then gave him the banner, and Allah granted conquest through him. And I was among those who stretched their necks toward it."
"1745","On the authority of Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, who said: While we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) among nearly eighty men from Quraysh, none of whom was other than a Qurashi—by Allah, I never saw the visages of men more handsome than their faces on that day—they mentioned women and spoke about them, and he spoke with them until I wished he would fall silent. He said: Then he came to me, recited the tashahhud, then said: ""As for what follows: O people of Quraysh! You are the people of this matter as long as you do not disobey Allah; but if you disobey Him, He will send against you one who will contend with you as this rod contends with another rod in his hand."" Then he struck his rod, and behold, it was white, shining."
"1746","[AI-translation] 'Irbad bin Sariyah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) exhorted us after the morning prayer with an eloquent exhortation, from which the eyes shed tears and the hearts trembled. A man among his companions said: O Messenger of Allah, it is as if this is the exhortation of one bidding farewell. He said: I enjoin you to fear Allah, and to hear and obey, even if a slave from Abyssinia. For whoever lives among you after me will see much disagreement. So hold fast to my Sunnah and the Sunnah of the Rightly Guided Caliphs after me. Bite onto it with the molars. And beware of newly invented matters, for every newly invented matter is an innovation, and every innovation is misguidance."
"1747","[AI-translation] From Ibn 'Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: The beginning of this affair is prophethood and mercy, then it will be caliphate and mercy, then it will be kingship and mercy, then they will push one another for it like the pushing of donkeys. So upon you is Jihad, and the best of your Jihad is Ribat, and the best of your Ribat is 'Asqalan."
"1748","Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah reported that Aisha said: When the Prophet ﷺ became seriously ill and his pain intensified, he asked permission from his wives to be nursed in my house, and they granted him permission. The Prophet ﷺ came out between two men, his feet dragging on the ground, between Abbas and another man. Ubaydullah said: I informed Ibn Abbas about this, and he said: ""Do you know who the other man was?"" I said: ""No."" He said: ""It was Ali.""Aisha used to narrate that the Prophet ﷺ said—after he entered his house and his pain intensified: ""Pour upon me from seven water skins that have not had their cords untied, so that I may give counsel to the people."" He was seated in a tub belonging to Hafsa, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ. Then we began pouring that water on him until he gestured to us that: ""You have done enough."" Then he went out to the people."
"1749","[AI-translation] Awar al-Sulami, raised to the Prophet: Beware of the doors of the sultan, for it has become difficult to descend."
"1750","[AI-translation] From Maqil bin Yasar who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: Any shepherd who is entrusted with a flock and deceives it, he is in the Fire."
"1751","[AI-translation] Samit who said: We pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, to hear and obey in hardship and ease, in willingness and reluctance, and to endure favoritism against us, and not to dispute the matter with its people (: except if you see open disbelief for which you have a proof from Allah), and to speak the truth wherever we are, not fearing in Allah the blame of any blamer."
"1752","Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh reported: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ remained in Mecca for ten years, following people in their dwellings during the seasons of ʿUkāẓ, Majanna, and the gatherings at Minā, saying: ""Who will give me shelter? Who will support me until I convey the message of my Lord, and for him is Paradise?"" Until a man would come from Yemen or from Muḍar — so he said — and his people would come to him and say: ""Beware of the youth of Quraysh, lest he seduce you."" And he would walk among their camps while they pointed at him with their fingers. Until Allah sent us to him from Yathrib; we gave him shelter and believed in him. Then a man from among us would go out, believe in him, and learn the Qurʾān from him, then return to his people, and they would embrace Islam through his Islam. Until there remained no dwelling of the Anṣār except that it contained a group of Muslims openly practicing Islam. Then they consulted together and said: ""Until when shall we leave the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to be driven out in the mountains of Mecca and live in fear?"" So seventy men from among us set out for him until they reached him during the season. We appointed to meet him at the mountain pass of al-ʿAqaba. We gathered there, man by man, two by two, until we had all assembled. We said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Shall we pledge allegiance to you?"" He said: ""You pledge allegiance to me upon hearing and obeying in energy and weariness, spending in hardship and ease, enjoining good and forbidding evil, and that you speak the truth for the sake of Allah, not fearing the blame of any critic. And that you support me and protect me when I come to you as you protect yourselves, your wives, and your children. And for you is Paradise."" He said: So we stood up and pledged allegiance to him. And al-Barāʾ ibn Maʿrūr — and he was among the youngest of them — took his hand and said: ""Gently, O people of Yathrib! For by Allah, we have not beaten the flanks of our camels except while knowing that he is the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. And his expulsion today means separation from all the Arabs, the killing of your best, and that swords will bite you. So either you are a people who endure that, and your reward is with Allah, or you are a people who fear for yourselves cowardice; then make that clear, for it is an excuse for you before Allah."" They said: ""Remove your hand from us, O Saʿd! By Allah, we will never abandon this pledge, nor will we ever renounce it."" He said: So we stood up and pledged allegiance to him, and he took the pledge from us and stipulated the conditions, and promised us Paradise in return."
"1753","[AI-translation] Samit, raised to the Prophet: Come, pledge allegiance to me upon that you will not associate anything with Allah, nor steal, nor commit fornication, nor kill your children, nor utter slander fabricating it between your hands and your feet, nor disobey me in what is good. So whoever fulfills this among you, his reward is upon Allah. And whoever commits any of that and is punished for it in this world, it is an expiation for him. And whoever commits any of that and Allah conceals it for him, his matter is up to Allah; if He wills, He will punish him, and if He wills, He will forgive him."
"1754","On the authority of An-Nu'man ibn Bashir, who said: We were sitting in the mosque, and Bashir was a man who restrained his speech. Then Abu Tha'labah al-Khushani came and said: ""O Bashir ibn Sa'd! Do you preserve the hadith of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) regarding the rulers?"" Hudhayfah said: ""I preserve his sermon."" So Abu Tha'labah sat down. Hudhayfah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) said: ""Prophethood will remain among you for as long as Allah wills it to remain, then Allah will raise it up when He wills to raise it up. Then there will be a Caliphate upon the methodology of Prophethood, so it will remain for as long as Allah wills it to remain, then He will raise it up when He wills to raise it up. Then there will be a biting kingship, so it will remain for as long as Allah wills it to remain, then He will raise it up when He wills to raise it up. Then there will be a coercive kingship, so it will remain for as long as Allah wills it to remain, then He will raise it up when He wills to raise it up. Then there will be a Caliphate upon the methodology of Prophethood."" Then he fell silent."
"1755","[AI-translation] From Abdullah bin Hawalah who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said one day: You will descend upon a man wearing a striped cloak, pledging to the people of Paradise. So we descended upon Uthman bin Affan, and he was wearing a striped cloak, pledging to the people. He said: meaning buying and selling."
"1756","[AI-translation] From Salman, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: Three will not enter Paradise: the fornicating old man, the lying imam, and the destitute who is arrogant."
"1757","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, he said: Three whose supplications Allah does not reject: the one who remembers Allah much, the supplication of the oppressed, and the just imam."
"1758","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family: Three whom Allah will not speak to on the Day of Resurrection, nor will He look at them, nor will He purify them, and they will have a painful punishment: a man who has surplus water in a desert and withholds it from the wayfarer, a man who bargained with another man over goods after the Asr prayer and swore by Allah that he had bought it for such and such, so he believed him while it was otherwise, and a man who pledged allegiance to an imam only for worldly gain; if he is given from it, he fulfills, and if he is not given from it, he does not fulfill."
"1759","On the authority of Abū Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) set out for Khaybar when he appointed Sibaʿ ibn ʿUrfuṭah over Medina. Abū Hurayrah said: I arrived in Medina as an emigrant and prayed the dawn prayer behind Sibaʿ. He recited in the first rakʿah: ""Kāf Hā Yā ʿAyn Ṣād"" (Maryam: 1), and in the second rakʿah: ""Woe to the defrauders"" (Al-Muṭaffifīn: 1). Abū Hurayrah said: So I said to myself during the prayer: ""Woe to the father of so-and-so! He has two measures: when he receives by measure, he takes in full, but when he gives by measure, he gives short."" When we finished our prayer, we went to Sibaʿ and he provisioned us with something until we reached the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), who had conquered Khaybar. He addressed the Muslims, so they gave us a share in their portions."
"1760","[AI-translation] Ashja'i, raised to the Prophet: The best of your imams are those whom you love and who love you, and who pray for you and you pray for them, and the worst of your imams are those whom you hate and who hate you, and whom you curse and who curse you. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, should we not fight them with the sword? He said: No, as long as they establish prayer among you. And if you see from your rulers something you dislike, hate their action, but do not withdraw a hand from obedience."
"1761","[AI-translation] Rahman, the freed slave of the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, raised to the Prophet: The caliphate will be thirty years, then it will become kingship after that."
"1762","[AI-translation] Narrated from 'Utbah bin 'Abd Allah, elevated to the Prophet: The caliphate is in Quraysh, the rule is in the Ansar, the call is in Al-Habashah, and the emigration is among the Muslims and the emigrants afterwards."
"1763","[AI-translation] Zubayr who said: I asked Jabir about the affair of Thaqif when they pledged allegiance? He said: They made a condition upon the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) that there would be no sadaqah upon them and no jihad. He said: And Jabir informed me that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) said: ""They will give sadaqah and wage jihad once they embrace Islam."
"1764","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Hurayrah: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: There will be caliphs after me who act upon what they know and do what they are commanded, and there will be caliphs after me who act upon what they do not know and do what they are not commanded. So whoever denounces them is absolved, and whoever withholds his hand is safe, but whoever is pleased and follows."
"1765","[AI-translation] Samit, elevated to the Prophet: There will be rulers after me who will make you recognize what you reject, and reject upon you what you recognize. So whoever among you attains that, there is no obedience to one who disobeys Allah."
"1766","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Hurayrah: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) said: Obedience to the Imam is a right upon the Muslim man as long as he does not command disobedience to Allah, the Mighty and Sublime. But if he commands disobedience to Allah, then there is no obedience to him."
"1767","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 1767 Arabic Hadees:"
"1768","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Dharr: I was walking arm-in-arm with the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) one day to his house, and I heard him say: Other than the Dajjal, I fear more for my Ummah than the Dajjal: the misleading imams."
"1769","On the authority of Hudhayfah, he said: The people used to ask the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) about good, but I used to ask him about evil out of fear that it might reach me. So I said: ""O Messenger of Allah, we were in ignorance and evil, then Allah brought us this good (and we are in it), (and He brought you). Will there be any evil after this good (as there was before it)?"" He said: ""O Hudhayfah! Learn the Book of Allah and follow what is in it,"" (three times). I said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Will there be good after this evil?"" He said: ""Yes."" (I said: ""What is the protection from it?"" He said: ""The sword."") I said: ""And will there be evil after that good?"" (And in a narration: ""I said: 'And will there be any remnant after the sword?'"") He said: ""Yes, and in it (and in a narration: 'There will be an emirate (and in a wording: a group) upon... and a truce upon') smoke (dakhan)."" I said: ""And what is its dakhan?"" He said: ""A people (and in another narration: 'There will be after me Imams (who follow other than my Sunnah, and) guide with other than my guidance; you will recognize from them and deny (and there will arise among them men whose hearts are the hearts of devils, in human bodies).')"" (And in another: ""The truce upon dakhan, what is it?"" He said: ""The hearts of a people will not return to what they were upon."") I said: ""Then will there be evil after that good?"" He said: ""Yes, (a blind and deaf fitnah, upon it) are callers at the gates of Hell; whoever answers them to it, they will throw him into it."" I said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Describe them to us."" He said: ""They are from our skin (i.e., our people) and speak with our tongues."" I said: ""(O Messenger of Allah) Then what do you command me if I reach that?"" He said: ""Adhere to the Jama'ah ("
"1770","[AI-translation] Narrated from 'Abd Allah bin 'Amr: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) would not shake hands with women during the pledge of allegiance."
"1771","[AI-translation] Samit, elevated to the Prophet: He would take a piece of wool from the side of a camel from the spoils of war, then say: ""I have in it nothing but the likes of what any one of you has."" Then he would say: ""Beware of ghulul, for ghulul is disgrace upon its possessor on the Day of Resurrection. Render the thread and the needle and what is beyond that, and strive in the cause of Allah, the near and the far, in residence and in travel, for jihad is a gate from the gates of Paradise; Allah saves its companion from worry and grief. And establish the limits of Allah regarding the near and the far, and let not the blame of a blamer deter you concerning Allah."
"1772","[AI-translation] Khattab: The Prophet (peace be upon him) used to converse at night with Abu Bakr concerning matters of the Muslims' affairs, and I was with them."
"1773","On the authority of Jubayr ibn Nufayr, who said: We were encamped with Mu'awiyah after the killing of 'Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him). Ka'b ibn Murrah al-Bahzi stood up and said: ""Were it not for something I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), I would not have stood in this position."" When Mu'awiyah heard the mention of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he made the people sit down and said: ""While we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), 'Uthman ibn 'Affan (may Allah be pleased with him) passed by, walking with a staff. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: 'A fitnah will surely emerge from beneath the feet of this one — or from between his legs —' meaning 'Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him). 'This one on that day, and whoever follows him, will be upon guidance.'""Ibn Hawalah al-Azdi stood up from near the pulpit and said: ""Are you the one who witnessed this?"" He said: ""Yes."" He said: ""By Allah, I was present at that gathering, and had I known that there was someone in the army who would corroborate me, I would have been the first to speak of it."""
"1774","[AI-translation] Khudri from the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family): For every betrayer there is a flag on the Day of Resurrection by which he will be recognized at his buttocks."
"1775","[AI-translation] From Abu Sa'id and Abu Hurairah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: There will come over you rulers who bring near the evildoers and delay the prayer from its appointed times. So whoever encounters that from them, let him not be an 'arif, nor a shurti, nor a jabbi, nor a khazin."
"1776","[AI-translation] From Shaddad bin Aws, from the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, raised: The evildoers of this Ummah will surely be carried upon the way of those who passed before them from the People of the Book, as exactly as a feather matches a feather."
"1777","[AI-translation] Dahhak bin Qays sent with him a garment to Marwan bin al-Hakam. Marwan said to the doorkeeper: See who is at the door? He said: Abu Hurairah. So he gave him permission. He said: O Abu Hurairah, narrate to us something you heard from the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, say: A man will soon wish that he had fallen from the Pleiades, and he had not assumed any matter of the people."
"1778","[AI-translation] Dahhak bin Qays sent with him a garment to Marwan bin al-Hakam. Marwan said to the doorkeeper: See who is at the door? He said: Abu Hurairah. So he gave him permission. He said: O Abu Hurairah, narrate to us something you heard from the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, say: A man will surely soon wish that he had fallen from the Pleiades, and he had not assumed any matter of the people."
"1779","[AI-translation] From Amr bin Murrah who said: I said to Mu'awiyah bin Sufyan: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, say: There is no Imam who closes his door against those with need, poverty, and destitution except that Allah closes the gates of heaven against his need, poverty, and destitution."
"1780","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet, peace be upon him: There is no commander of ten except that he will be brought on the Day of Resurrection bound in fetters; nothing will release him except justice, or injustice will ruin him."
"1781","[AI-translation] From Abu Umamah, from the Prophet, peace be upon him, that he said: There is no man who assumes authority over ten or more except that he will come to Allah, Mighty and Majestic, on the Day of Resurrection bound in fetters, his hand tied to his neck. His righteousness will release him, or his sin will ruin him. Its beginning is blame, its middle is regret, and its end is disgrace on the Day of Resurrection."
"1782","[AI-translation] Hasan who said: Ubaidullah bin Ziyad visited Maqil bin Yasar al-Muzani during the illness in which he died. Maqil said: I am narrating to you a hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him. Had I known that I would have life, I would not have narrated it to you. I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, say: There is no servant whom Allah places in charge of a flock who dies on the day he dies while he is deceitful to his flock, except that Allah forbids Paradise to him."
"1783","[AI-translation] From Abdullah bin Buraidah, from his father, raised: No people ever break the covenant except that killing occurs among them, and immorality never appears among a people except that Allah sends death upon them, and no people withhold Zakah except that Allah withholds rain from them."
"1784","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah, raised: Whoever leaves obedience and separates from the community, and dies, dies a death of Jahiliyyah. And whoever fights under a banner of blind fanaticism, getting angry for partisanship, or calling to partisanship, or supporting partisanship, and is killed, is killed a death of Jahiliyyah. And whoever goes out against my Ummah, striking its righteous and its wicked, not sparing its believers, and not fulfilling the covenant of those with a covenant, is not from me, and I am not from him."
"1785","[AI-translation] Narrated Ibn 'Umar, raised to the Prophet: Whoever withdraws a hand from obedience will meet Allah on the Day of Resurrection having no excuse for him, and whoever dies while there is no pledge of allegiance on his neck dies a death of Jahiliyyah."
"1786","[AI-translation] Bajali, raised to the Prophet: Whoever is killed under a blind banner, calling to tribalism or supporting tribalism, is killed a death of Jahiliyyah."
"1787","[AI-translation] Qasim bin Muhammad who said: I heard my aunt ('Aishah) say: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: Whoever of you is put in charge of a task and Allah intends good for him, He will appoint for him a righteous minister who reminds him if he forgets and helps him if he remembers."
"1788","Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: ""O Messenger of Allah, you are dearer to me than myself, and you are dearer to me than my family, and dearer to me than my children. And when I am in my house, I remember you and I cannot bear it until I come to you and look at you. And when I remember my death and your death, I know that when you enter Paradise, you will be raised with the prophets, and I fear that when I enter Paradise, I will not see you."" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not reply to him until Jibreel came down with this verse: ""And whoever obeys Allah and the Messenger - those will be with the ones upon whom Allah has bestowed favor of the prophets, the steadfast affirmers of truth, the martyrs and the righteous. And excellent are those as companions."" (An-Nisa: 69)"
"1789","[AI-translation] Narrated Mujashi' bin Mas'ud that he came to the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, with a nephew of his to pledge allegiance to him for migration. The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, said: No, rather he should pledge allegiance to Islam, for there is no migration after the Conquest, and he will be among the Followers."
"1790","[AI-translation] Narrated 'Imran bin Husayn who narrated from the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, that he said: There is no obedience in the disobedience of Allah, Blessed and Exalted."
"1791","On the authority of Abdullah ibn al-Samit, who said: Ziyad wanted to appoint Imran ibn Husayn as governor over Khurasan, but he refused. His companions said to him: ""Did you leave Khurasan so that you could be its governor?"" He said: ""By Allah, it would not please me that I should pray in its heat while you pray in its coolness. And I fear that if I were in the thick of battle against the enemy, a letter from Ziyad would come to me; if I proceeded, I would perish, and if I returned, my neck would be struck."" Then he wanted to appoint al-Hakam ibn Amr al-Ghifari over it, and he complied with his command. Imran said: ""Is there no one to call al-Hakam for me?"" The messenger went, and al-Hakam came to him and entered. Imran said to al-Hakam: ""Did you hear the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) say: 'There is no obedience to anyone in disobedience to Allah, Blessed and Exalted'?"" He said: ""Yes."" Imran said: ""Praise be to Allah,"" or ""Allah is Greatest."""
"1792","[AI-translation] Narrated 'Ali: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, sent an army and appointed a man over them. He lit a fire and said: Enter it. So some people intended to enter it, and others said: We have fled from it. This was mentioned to the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, so he said to those who intended to enter it: Had you entered it, you would have remained in it until the Day of Resurrection. And he spoke good words to the others, and said: There is no obedience (to a human) in the disobedience of Allah; rather, obedience is only in what is good."
"1793","[AI-translation] Ghifari who said: We entered upon 'Ali bin Abi Talib on the day of al-Adha, and he presented to us a broth. We said: O Amir al-Mu'minin! If only you presented to us of this duck and bustard, for there is much good. He said: O Ibn Zarir, I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, say: It is not lawful for the Caliph except for two bowls: a bowl which he and his family eat, and a bowl which he feeds to others."
"1794","[AI-translation] Narrated Jabir bin Samurah, raised to the Prophet: This matter will remain mighty until twelve caliphs, all of them from Quraysh."
"1795","[AI-translation] Narrated 'Abdullah bin 'Amr, raised to the Prophet: This matter will remain in Quraysh as long as two people remain from mankind."
"1796","[AI-translation] Narrated Mu'awiyah bin Abi Sufyan who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, say: There will be rulers, and their words will not be rejected; they will plunge into the Fire, following one another."
"1797","On the authority of Abu Nadrah, who said: We were with Jabir ibn Abdullah when he said: ""The people of Iraq will soon have no qafiz nor dirham brought to them."" We asked: ""From where will that be?"" He said: ""From the direction of the non-Arabs, who will prevent that."" Then he said: ""The people of Syria will soon have no dinar nor mudd brought to them."" We asked: ""From where will that be?"" He said: ""From the direction of the Romans, who will prevent that."" He said: Then he paused for a moment, then said: ""The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: 'There will be at the end of my Ummah a Caliph who will scatter wealth profusely, not counting it.'"" He said: I said to Abu Nadrah and Abu Al-Ala: ""Do you two think that it is Umar ibn Abdul Aziz?"" They both said: ""No."""
